    "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23404801",
    "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23404802",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "S07 Pre-registration \u2014 Protocol for the Benchmark-Practice Inflation Study",
      "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23404802",
      "publication_date": "2026-10-15",
      "description": "<p>Protocol declaration and locked artifacts for S07. Declared before any model was fit.</p>\n<p>Contents: cohort derivation rules from the S04 OpenML snapshot, the confirmatory family (H1, H2&times;3, H4&times;3), the SESOI (0.02 bAcc), the pre-declared decision rules, and the exact identity Delta_conv = Delta_mat + Delta_thr.</p>\n<p>Protocol SHA-256: c78b78ed48ea3e00d1e1c9f63ace246485fff8657164061aded5fdeb8febd525</p>\n<p>The S07 study measures how much of the reported benefit of class-imbalance correction over a plain classifier is an artifact of the default 0.5 decision threshold of the control. The unit of claim is the benchmark practice; the system NeuroCortex-SRDF appears only as one documented instance of that practice. Cohort R: 131 OpenML binary tabular datasets. Declared status: confirmatory (N_req = 70).</p>",
      "access_right": "open",
      "creators": [
        {
          "name": "Al-Athwary, Mohammed Qaid",
          "affiliation": null,
          "orcid": "0009-0006-9075-072X"
        }
      ],
